{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03678",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 4.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "hello, doctor may I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.13,
      "end_seconds": 9.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.35,
      "end_seconds": 24.75,
      "duration_seconds": 14.4,
      "text": "well, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening. Well, it's a bump on the head yesterday, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.09,
      "end_seconds": 29.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.07,
      "end_seconds": 33.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Since this morning, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.97,
      "end_seconds": 38.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Mm, okay. So, any a mild headache as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.64,
      "end_seconds": 52.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "yes, I have. As for feeling fine otherwise, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 53.99,
      "end_seconds": 63.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 69 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 36.6 degrees, BP is 120 over 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.98,
      "end_seconds": 65.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.14,
      "end_seconds": 70.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.49,
      "end_seconds": 74.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.1,
      "end_seconds": 99.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "you are alert and orientated with a small bruise on the forehead and normal limb strength"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.18,
      "end_seconds": 107.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.67,
      "end_seconds": 121.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.67,
      "end_seconds": 126.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Actually, no, I haven't had any vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 128.08,
      "end_seconds": 133.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice vomiting. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.24,
      "end_seconds": 141.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.36,
      "end_seconds": 151.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed have you noticed confusion, drowsiness or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.35,
      "end_seconds": 156.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "No, um, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.68,
      "end_seconds": 161.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.33,
      "end_seconds": 164.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "bowels are regular, nothing odd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.72,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.24,
      "end_seconds": 172.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Well, I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.43,
      "end_seconds": 178.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.56,
      "end_seconds": 184.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.88,
      "end_seconds": 187.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.7,
      "end_seconds": 191.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I've, I've had gout, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.58,
      "end_seconds": 201.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat and gout are known to us, good to have that clear. Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.56,
      "end_seconds": 205.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.68,
      "end_seconds": 209.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.15,
      "end_seconds": 214.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.35,
      "end_seconds": 220.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Alright, do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.44,
      "end_seconds": 225.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.54,
      "end_seconds": 228.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.07,
      "end_seconds": 238.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day. I take a blood thinner, 5 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.39,
      "end_seconds": 242.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.97,
      "end_seconds": 248.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Yes, I had my septum straightened, in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.18,
      "end_seconds": 253.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.19,
      "end_seconds": 260.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia. Erm, my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.4,
      "end_seconds": 297.7,
      "duration_seconds": 21.3,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? The most likely explanation is a minor head injury but on a blood thinner, which needs a scan we shouldn't forget a simple bump just to be sure I understood you've had a bump on the head yesterday, since this morning, and no seizure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.1,
      "end_seconds": 301.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "right, yes, you've got it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.36,
      "end_seconds": 326.92,
      "duration_seconds": 15.56,
      "text": "I'm going to order a CT scan of the head, for head injury on anticoagulant even though you feel fine, a blood thinner means we scan, delayed bleeding can happen please come and see me today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.51,
      "end_seconds": 330.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.96,
      "end_seconds": 335.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Alright, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.75,
      "end_seconds": 342.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Alright, uh, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}